[{:db/id "78c86cc8-66c7-50dd-9fc4-ded5ae059599" :answer/id #uuid "78c86cc8-66c7-50dd-9fc4-ded5ae059599" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2 t + 1" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "d9187c94-57be-571f-b824-8290c0c50c00" :answer/id #uuid "d9187c94-57be-571f-b824-8290c0c50c00" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t \\left(t - 1\\right)" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "0508161d-0559-5c9c-94b0-dabbf30c8892" :answer/id #uuid "0508161d-0559-5c9c-94b0-dabbf30c8892" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2 t - 1" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "d334b550-3042-553b-b847-e1e7fe52d626" :answer/id #uuid "d334b550-3042-553b-b847-e1e7fe52d626" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2 \\left(t - 1\\right)" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "09f295d9-03a2-5561-bbef-04c9bb89034c" :answer/id #uuid "09f295d9-03a2-5561-bbef-04c9bb89034c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "844dfb74-8a60-5fe0-bb44-50294978c57a" :answer-field/id #uuid "844dfb74-8a60-5fe0-bb44-50294978c57a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["78c86cc8-66c7-50dd-9fc4-ded5ae059599" "d9187c94-57be-571f-b824-8290c0c50c00" "0508161d-0559-5c9c-94b0-dabbf30c8892" "d334b550-3042-553b-b847-e1e7fe52d626" "09f295d9-03a2-5561-bbef-04c9bb89034c"] :answer-field/correct "0508161d-0559-5c9c-94b0-dabbf30c8892" :db/ensure :answer-field/validate} {:db/id "fbb4e13f-d8a8-5c5d-b9d1-448311f2dde4" :question/id #uuid "fbb4e13f-d8a8-5c5d-b9d1-448311f2dde4" :question/problem "If $f(x,y,z)=x + y - 2 z$ and $r(t)=(t)\\,i+(t^{2})\\,j+(t)\\,k,$ compute $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))].$" :question/worked-solution "The chain rule in vector form states that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))]=∇f(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t).\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to compute $∇f(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(x + y - 2 z)\\,i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(x + y - 2 z)\\,j+\\frac{∂}{∂z}(x + y - 2 z)\\,k \\\\  & =(1)\\,i+(1)\\,j+(-2)\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute $x=t,y=t^{2},$ and $z=t$ into the above to find $∇f(r(t)):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(r(t)) & =(1)\\,i+(1)\\,j+(-2)\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate the derivative of $r(t),$ which is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t^{2})\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)\\,k \\\\  & =(1)\\,i+(2 t)\\,j+(1)\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, applying the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))] & =∇f(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =((1)\\,i+(1)\\,j+(-2)\\,k)\\cdot ((1)\\,i+(2 t)\\,j+(1)\\,k) \\\\  & =(1)\\cdot (1)+(1)\\cdot (2 t)+(-2)\\cdot (1) \\\\  & =(1)+(2 t)+(-2) \\\\  & =2 t - 1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["844dfb74-8a60-5fe0-bb44-50294978c57a"] :db/ensure :question/validate} {:db/id "a9e4f8f2-4f25-544c-a9ba-33e2472e1343" :answer/id #uuid "a9e4f8f2-4f25-544c-a9ba-33e2472e1343" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "- 2 t" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "326ed290-c2d9-50d2-88c8-74db06917de4" :answer/id #uuid "326ed290-c2d9-50d2-88c8-74db06917de4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "- t \\left(t + 1\\right)" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "4db710c0-beac-5a6e-854d-7b7866f60c72" :answer/id #uuid "4db710c0-beac-5a6e-854d-7b7866f60c72" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "- (2 t + 1)" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "336c3865-f674-544a-82cb-712e32c64648" :answer/id #uuid "336c3865-f674-544a-82cb-712e32c64648" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "- (6 t + 1)" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "56a00959-2111-50b5-b5fe-ba2f85d7c3bb" :answer/id #uuid "56a00959-2111-50b5-b5fe-ba2f85d7c3bb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4 t - 1" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "32e468ca-2d16-55b6-a084-1a0ff8b6f7f2" :answer-field/id #uuid "32e468ca-2d16-55b6-a084-1a0ff8b6f7f2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["a9e4f8f2-4f25-544c-a9ba-33e2472e1343" "326ed290-c2d9-50d2-88c8-74db06917de4" "4db710c0-beac-5a6e-854d-7b7866f60c72" "336c3865-f674-544a-82cb-712e32c64648" "56a00959-2111-50b5-b5fe-ba2f85d7c3bb"] :answer-field/correct "4db710c0-beac-5a6e-854d-7b7866f60c72" :db/ensure :answer-field/validate} {:db/id "11cc55a9-a3be-504c-b916-0f019947db61" :question/id #uuid "11cc55a9-a3be-504c-b916-0f019947db61" :question/problem "If $f(x,y,z)=- x - 3 y + 2 z$ and $r(t)=(t)\\,i+(t^{2})\\,j+(t^{2})\\,k,$ compute $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))].$" :question/worked-solution "The chain rule in vector form states that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))]=∇f(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t).\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to compute $∇f(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(- x - 3 y + 2 z)\\,i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(- x - 3 y + 2 z)\\,j+\\frac{∂}{∂z}(- x - 3 y + 2 z)\\,k \\\\  & =(-1)\\,i+(-3)\\,j+(2)\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute $x=t,y=t^{2},$ and $z=t^{2}$ into the above to find $∇f(r(t)):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(r(t)) & =(-1)\\,i+(-3)\\,j+(2)\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate the derivative of $r(t),$ which is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t^{2})\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t^{2})\\,k \\\\  & =(1)\\,i+(2 t)\\,j+(2 t)\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, applying the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))] & =∇f(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =((-1)\\,i+(-3)\\,j+(2)\\,k)\\cdot ((1)\\,i+(2 t)\\,j+(2 t)\\,k) \\\\  & =(-1)\\cdot (1)+(-3)\\cdot (2 t)+(2)\\cdot (2 t) \\\\  & =(-1)+(- 6 t)+(4 t) \\\\  & =- (2 t + 1).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["32e468ca-2d16-55b6-a084-1a0ff8b6f7f2"] :db/ensure :question/validate} {:db/id "cc2d2ded-87cd-520a-9927-cc57f85daf7c" :a